# List pagination (VCP)

When adding or changing a **list / index** page:

1. Use `LIST_PAGE_SIZE` (tables/rows) or `COMPANIES_PAGE_SIZE` (admin
   company cards) + helpers from `src/list_page.rs` (`?page=`, 1-based).
2. With filter chips: pager on the same `vb-chip-row` (right). Chip hrefs omit `page`.
3. Without chips: `vb-list-toolbar` above the table, pager right.
4. Pager = SSR `<a href>` only — no client JS pager.
5. Live-search shards take `page` and reset to 1 when the query signal changes.
6. Prefer Toasty SQL `.limit` / `.offset` / `.count` / filters — not
   `Model::all()` then `page_slice` (`toasty` skill).
7. **Exception — release catalogues:** after a SQL-bounded set (published
   + entitlement, or staff global catalogue), keep Rust
   `cmp_version_desc` + `page_slice`. Full SQL `ORDER BY version` breaks
   semver / client-suffix ordering until a `sort_key` column exists.
8. Ship the full test pyramid for that surface (see `web-stack` § List pagination).
